# v1.7 source-side normalization -- use this, not the old p-only formulation

Let A be the genuine triangle-free source minimizer, H=conv(A), |A|=N, diam(H)=D.
Define

\[
\widehat N_H=\alpha_1(H),
\qquad
\widehat p_H=\widehat N_H-N.
\]

Then

\[
0\le\widehat p_H\le p<\frac{\pi D}{2}.
\]

For every finite unit-separated Q subset H,

\[
\boxed{|Q|-|N_A(Q)|\le\widehat p_H.}
\]

This is now the authoritative fixed-source Hall bound.  Therefore a sufficient
source contradiction for the **existing fixed scaffold** is

\[
\boxed{
g>0
\Longrightarrow
\exists Q\subset H:
|Q|-|N_A(Q)|\ge\widehat p_H+1.
}
\]

Do NOT revert to p+1 as though it were still the sharp fixed-source threshold.

The exact self-container theorem also gives

\[
\alpha_1(\operatorname{int}H)\le N-1,
\]

so every (N+k)-point packing in H has at least k+1 points on the actual boundary.
Use this boundary reserve when relevant, but do not falsely infer that the newly
inserted Q itself must meet the boundary.

---

# Maximal triangle-free same-hull source extension

Define B as a maximum triangle-free extension of A inside H:

\[
A\subseteq B\subseteq H,
\qquad
|B|=q=N+k.
\]

Then

\[
D(q)=D,
\qquad
0\le k\le\widehat p_H.
\]

If R is the original strict-rattler set,

\[
|R_B|\ge |R|-5k,
\]

so a super-boundary rattler population remains super-boundary.

B is append-maximal in the triangle-free class and is closed-unit-covering in H:

\[
H\subseteq\bigcup_{b\in B}\overline B(b,1).
\]

Every unit-separated appendable position must be an equilateral apex of a unit edge
of B, and adding it necessarily creates a unit triangle.

Define

\[
\tau=\alpha_1(H)-|B|=\widehat p_H-k.
\]

Then

\[
\boxed{|Q|-|N_B(Q)|\le\tau.}
\]

If you replace A by B, you MUST rebuild the Target A scaffold.  Do not use the old S
as if it were the response matrix of B.  After the rebuild, a sufficient source
contradiction is

\[
\boxed{
g_B>0
\Longrightarrow
\exists Q\subset H:
|Q|-|N_B(Q)|\ge\tau+1.
}
\]

Do not assume tau=0.

