# Same-cardinality rattler-preserving saturation

You may normalize the genuine source to closed-unit-cover its original hull WITHOUT
adding O(D) points.

If y in H is at distance >1 from every current point, remove an endpoint x of a unit
contact and insert y.  The new set remains an N-point triangle-free global minimizer.
The inserted y has no unit contacts, so the contact count drops.  Iterating terminates.

Any specified original strict-rattler set R is kept pointwise and remains strict.
Therefore there exists a same-cardinality triangle-free global minimizer A_sat with

\[
H\subseteq\bigcup_{a\in A_{\rm sat}}\overline B(a,1)
\]

and the original super-boundary R intact.

Do not use this representative simultaneously with the old hybrid core/forest unless
you separately rebuild and audit that normal form; the replacement sequence can alter
the contact graph.

This theorem may remove boundary-order normalization losses from arguments that need
only source saturation and rattlers.

