# Capacity shadow: bounded-displacement same-cardinality optimum partner

For the genuine source A and any capacity endpoint X_max, the saturating matching
produces an injection

\[
\mu:A\hookrightarrow X_{\max},
\qquad
|a-\mu(a)|<1.
\]

Let Y=mu(A).  Then Y is another N-point global optimum of diameter D.

If L=conv(Y) and

\[
\delta=\max_a|a-\mu(a)|<1,
\]

then

\[
\boxed{L\subseteq H\subseteq L+\delta B,}
\]

so

\[
d_H(H,L)<1,
\qquad
0\le P_H-P_L<2\pi.
\]

This is the first exact pointwise coupling of the source to another globally optimal
configuration inside a source capacity endpoint.

Try to transport this finite chord through deletion of the strict-rattler population
toward the smaller plateau endpoint.  A successful transport that creates s
independent boundary null directions of the Schur response would close Target A.

