# Binding regressions and prohibited shortcuts

Do NOT claim any of the following without a new proof:

- p=0, widehat p_H=0, or tau=0;
- source capacity bookkeeping alone gives tau+1 deficiency;
- maximal triangle-free extension preserves the old hybrid contact graph;
- every intermediate exchange-flag optimum is triangle-free;
- tree circuit means triangle-free sequentialization;
- source and smaller optimum are coordinate-identified;
- planarity alone implies the Target A separator saving;
- all alternating paths live in a width-one annulus;
- the response matrix is a DAG after arbitrary dimer contraction unless the exact
  phase-anchor construction is being used;
- individual Voronoi cells have area at least a_0;
- Oler defect is monotone between arbitrary cardinalities;
- distributed strain has a uniform density gap;
- long obtuse or straight runs are automatically Schuermann loose edges;
- a local/KKT theorem can see strict-rattler coordinates to finite order;
- Kuperberg's infinite gap-defect theorem directly applies to the finite scaffold;
- Bondarenko--Hardin--Saff mesh-ratio <=1 applies to every best-packing representative;
- Gensane's general strong-generator statement is proved.

Keep the strained-monomer, regular-shell, long rooted-chain, overlapping-circuit,
zero-charge-bulk, and annular-routing regressions active throughout the proof audit.

