Do not give a survey.  Work aggressively toward a proof.

If you obtain a new theorem, state it exactly, prove it fully, and immediately test it
against all relevant regressions.

If you believe Target A is closed, explicitly derive

\[
\dim\ker S\ge\Delta_\Lambda-d_{\rm int}
\]

or an exact source contradiction exceeding the appropriate fixed-hull Hall slack.
Do not hide the final one-integer implication behind an O(D), asymptotic, generic, or
"can be arranged" statement.

If full closure still fails, report only genuinely new rigorous progress, the exact
remaining implication, and any new failed route worth preserving.  Do not pad the
answer with old results already in v1.7.0.

Target B remains frozen unless it directly closes Target A.
